A: From the code you've shown, it seems that you want to test the Contains method of the ArrayList class using PEX.
To test the Contains method, you've declared a partial class and defined a method named PUT_ContainsContract. However, it appears that some of the parameters and assertions are missing in the code you've shared.

To test the Contains method properly, you'll need to populate the parameters and assertions correctly. Here's an example of how you can do it:

```csharp
partial class ArrayListContractTest
{
    public void PUT_ContainsContract([PexAssumeUnderTest] ArrayList arrList, int x)
    {
        // Assume preconditions
        AssumePrecondition.IsNotNull(arrList);

        // Save the initial state
        int initialCount = arrList.Count;
        int initialIndex = arrList.IndexOf(x);
        int initialLastIndex = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

        // Call the method
        bool contains = arrList.Contains(x);

        // Check postconditions
        Assert.IsTrue(contains);
        Assert.IsTrue(initialCount == arrList.Count); // Count should stay the same
        Assert.AreEqual(initialIndex, arrList.IndexOf(x)); // IndexOf() should stay the same or increase
        Assert.AreEqual(initialLastIndex, arrList.LastIndexOf(x)); // LastIndexOf() should stay the same or increase
    }
}
```

In this example, we assume that the `arrList` parameter is not null. Then we save the initial count, index, and last index of `x` in the ArrayList. After calling the Contains method, we check the postconditions by asserting that the return value is true (the item is in the ArrayList), and that the initial and final counts, indices, and last indices are the same or have increased appropriately.

You can modify the parameters and assertions based on your specific requirements. Let me know if you need any further assistance.--------------------            if (!New_Ret)
            {
                // The precondition is satisfied under the 'arrList' object
                Assume.Condition(() => arrList != null);
            //  Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_arrListIndexOfX); // Index cannot go up
		Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListLastIndexOfX <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX); 
            }
	// The precondition is satisfied under the 'arrList' object
            Assume.Condition(() => arrList != null);
        }
    }
}
```

